Heat flux, calorimetry, guarding and energy accounting (@th-heat-flux-measurement: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/Heat-Flux-Sensor-Calibration-NIST.lingua#r_6RP9VC0545310FNGXY9B50PN16", #source "../sources/Guarded-Hot-Plate-and-SRM-1450e-NIST.lingua#r_1PP28H0Y6N7RVY89W9HSQY18E4", #source "../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../../../inquiry/metrology/applications/Optical-and-imaging-measurements.lingua#r_5N7AJNW24YZV9CGHHEB0S6283T", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../research/Traceable-thermal-properties-and-radiation-measurements.lingua#r_6W5QAJWM3SCEDMD9WHNGJNS6DE") { r_0C5CNS266C7247SV38JME1TKPP
**Read:** [Heat-flux sensor calibration — NIST SP 250-65](../sources/Heat-Flux-Sensor-Calibration-NIST.lingua#r_6RP9VC0545310FNGXY9B50PN16), the complete calibration report; [Guarded-hot-plate evidence — NIST SP 260-201](../sources/Guarded-Hot-Plate-and-SRM-1450e-NIST.lingua#r_1PP28H0Y6N7RVY89W9HSQY18E4), guarding, balance and uncertainty; [Thermodynamics and Chemistry — Howard DeVoe](../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1), calorimetry and first-law measurement.

A heat-flux sensor samples a local interaction with its mounting and environment. Its reading is not automatically the total heat flow through an irregular surface. A calorimeter instead infers energy transfer from a carefully defined balance, often including electrical work, storage, loss and mass flow.

Derive the measurement equation for each method. Include sensor area, angular response where relevant, thermal shunting, contact, time response, radiation/convection conditions and calibration transfer. Map the spatial field before multiplying one flux reading by a whole area.

Compare a guarded steady experiment with a transient electrical-substitution or mixing account. Seek an independently measured energy closure rather than calibrating every unknown to force agreement. Report drift, equilibrium criteria and residuals. The complete NIST heat-flux calibration report supplies a primary method to scrutinize; it does not confer calibration on a sensor merely because its model number is familiar.

